# anthropic_plugin_marketplace_settings (Resource)

Manages the default installation setting of one of a Claude Enterprise organization's plugin marketplaces, through the [Plugins API](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/manage-claude/plugins-api#set-a-marketplaces-default-installation-setting): the organization-wide value of every plugin in the marketplace without a setting of its own, including plugins added later.

> **API**: `GET/POST /v1/organizations/plugin_marketplaces/{marketplace_id}` (Plugins API). No create or delete endpoint.
> **Auth**: Claude Enterprise Admin API key with the `read:plugins` and `write:plugins` scopes (`admin_api_key` / `ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_API_KEY`), created by the primary owner in claude.ai under Organization settings > API. A Claude Console Admin API key does not work.
> **Beta header**: `ce-plugins-2026-09-01`, sent by the provider (the endpoints answer 404 without it).
> **Availability**: beta, Claude Enterprise organizations only, and not organizations with HIPAA readiness enabled.
> **Cost**: Free.

## Behavior

- **Marketplaces are created, connected to a repository and deleted in claude.ai**, not through the API. Creating this resource adopts an existing marketplace of the organization (`manual` or synchronized from Git) and sets its default; find its ID in claude.ai or with `GET /v1/organizations/plugin_marketplaces`. A member's personal marketplace cannot be managed (403).
- **Destroy leaves the marketplace and its default as they are**, with a warning: a default can be changed but never removed. To leave a different default behind (`not_available`, the value of a marketplace whose default was never set, for example), apply it before removing the resource.
- A plugin's own `organization` setting (`anthropic_plugin_installation_setting`) overrides the marketplace default for that plugin.

